# Installed only on systems without a systemd user manager (Gentoo with OpenRC, FreeBSD), as
# /etc/greetd/sessions/wayland-sessions/hyprland.desktop. The greeter's XDG_DATA_DIRS lists
# /etc/greetd/sessions first, so ReGreet shows this entry instead of the package's
# hyprland.desktop (same relative name). There, nothing else starts a D-Bus session bus, which
# portals, notifications, the keyring and the polkit agent need.
[Desktop Entry]
Name=Hyprland
Comment=Hyprland with its own D-Bus session bus
Exec=dbus-run-session start-hyprland
Type=Application
DesktopNames=Hyprland
